This is a narrow backend smoke test, not product work. Do not inspect or
discover files, install anything, edit project files, or make a commit.

Use the normal SwarmForge handoff mechanism only. Its helper accepts a draft
file rather than positional `note` arguments, so run exactly this one harmless
command through your normal tool mechanism:

```sh
printf 'type: note\nto: smoke-vibe-coder\npriority: 50\nmessage: VIBE_TWO_PACK_OK\n' > .swarmforge/handoffs/outbox/tmp/vibe-smoke.handoff && swarmforge/scripts/swarm_handoff.sh .swarmforge/handoffs/outbox/tmp/vibe-smoke.handoff
```

This is the documented `swarm_handoff.sh` note path to
`smoke-vibe-coder` with marker `VIBE_TWO_PACK_OK`. If Vibe asks for approval,
show that exact command and stop; do not bypass the approval.
